GameLib steamclient-layer component - NOTICE

This component is downloaded by GameLib on the first DRM-mode launch of a
SteamStub title on macOS (D-05, D-18). It is published as one release asset
per allowlisted CrossOver build at
https://github.com/grayson-mitchell/GameLib/releases/tag/steamclient-layer-cx<build>
and is installed under GameLib's app-data directory
steam-bridge/drm/component/steamclient-layer-cx<build>/. It is not part of the
signed GameLib application, and GameLib verifies it against sha256 sums pinned
in that application before every use.

Licence of each file
--------------------

- lsteamclient.dll and lsteamclient.so: Steamworks SDK License. GameLib builds
  them from Proton lsteamclient at 164e0ccd2ea2b1ec2e5d08dc97f65b184c2539ca,
  with NotProton's three overlay files at
  8db22adb237e6ea640a5af148b69b93709daf50c and GameLib's trace additions,
  contributed under the same licence. The licence text is LICENSE.lsteamclient.
- detour-cx<build>.bin: GPL-3.0. It is ported from NotProton ntdll-patch.
- steam.exe: BSD-3-Clause. It is ported from NotProton steam-shim (Proton
  steam_helper).
- LICENSE.lsteamclient: Valve's Steamworks SDK License text, copied unmodified
  from Proton.
- NOTICE: this file.

Separation
----------

GameLib's GPL-3.0-only code never links against lsteamclient.dll or lsteamclient.so.
Wine loads those files at run time inside the game's Wine process, and no
GameLib process loads them. The GPL-3.0 detour payload is not linked with them
either: GameLib writes it into its own copy of CrossOver's ntdll.dll, where it
redirects the exports of Valve's genuine steamclient64.dll at run time.

Corresponding source
--------------------

For detour-cx<build>.bin and steam.exe: the GameLib repository at the commit
tagged steamclient-layer-cx<build>, under
native/steam-bridge/steamclient-layer/ntdll-patch/ (with COPYING, the GPL-3.0
text) and native/steam-bridge/steamclient-layer/helper/. They are built with
"pnpm build:drm-native" (meta/buildDrmNativeParts.ts). The lsteamclient overlay
and pins are in native/steam-bridge/steamclient-layer/lsteamclient/, built with
"pnpm build:lsteamclient". The archive is built with
"pnpm build:steamclient-layer-archive".

Not in this component
---------------------

Valve's steamclient64.dll, tier0_s64.dll and vstdlib_s64.dll. The user's
machine downloads those from Valve's own CDN; GameLib never distributes them
(D-04).

